This project explores how different factors influence a person's decision to accept a digital coupon while driving. 
As part of my Capstone in Integrative Data Analytics, I am working with a real-world dataset containing over 12,000 records.
So far, I have cleaned and prepared the data, handled missing values, and created new features such as income group and travel status. 
I have completed exploratory data analysis to identify trends and applied Principal Component Analysis (PCA) to reduce dimensionality while
keeping most of the meaningful information. The goal of this project is to understand consumer behavior in mobile settings and prepare the
data for future predictive modeling.
